6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:13,680
♫Always making that face whenever you see me♫

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,650
[7HD Channel]
♫Always making that face whenever you see me♫

8
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,480
[iQIYI]
♫Always making that face whenever you see me♫

9
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,580
♫What does that mean?♫

10
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,950
[Present]
♫What does that mean?♫

11
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:27,180
♫Whatever I say upset you, but you’ll get mad if I keep quiet♫

12
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:30,620
♫I really don’t know what to do♫

13
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:35,650
♫When deep down, I really like you♫

14
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:40,420
♫But you probably don’t care♫

15
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:43,480
♫Should I just say it out loud?♫

16
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:46,920
♫Or keep it all to myself and let it be?♫

17
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:49,320
♫What should I do?♫

18
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:54,120
♫I don’t know how to tell you how I feel♫

19
00:00:54,120 --> 00:01:00,150
♫I’m still confused by the way you react when I’m around♫

20
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:05,450
♫I’m still afraid. Will it be all right if I say it?♫

21
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:08,550
♫So I have to hide it inside♫

22
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:13,420
♫I don’t know what to do with these feelings♫

23
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:19,780
♫Always keep dreaming of you, night after night♫

24
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:24,620
♫What should I do? I can’t just let it go on like this♫

25
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:30,720
♫But I’m too afraid to say it, so I’ll just keep it to myself♫

26
00:01:32,479 --> 00:01:35,550
Flaming Chains of Love

27
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,700
[Previously]
You also hate her, don’t you?

28
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:39,380
I hate you a lot too!

29
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:40,920
Actually, I don’t hate you.

30
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:42,420
I like you.

31
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:43,720
Are you sure?

32
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:44,930
Yes.

33
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:47,580
But we’ve never had a good time together.

34
00:01:47,729 --> 00:01:49,380
Let’s go to the mountain together then.

35
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:51,680
Can you call me ‘Phi’ like when we were little?

36
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:52,880
Phi Jah.

37
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:54,530
Did you mean me?

38
00:01:54,930 --> 00:01:56,080
Of course.

39
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:00,220
Phi Jah, you’re the luckiest in the world!

40
00:02:01,650 --> 00:02:03,980
Holy shit! I’m sorry.

41
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:06,050
I didn’t see anything–didn’t see you and Miss Phrao kissing.

42
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:08,050
What if your aunt hears about it?

43
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:11,480
Nasty bitch! You know how much I hate her!

44
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,880
But I love her!

45
00:02:14,450 --> 00:02:15,220
Aunt Nee!

46
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,120
Miss Panee!

47
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,250
[Emergency Department]

48
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:24,120
Fai.

49
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,280
Dad!

50
00:02:30,270 --> 00:02:31,380
It’s all right.

51
00:02:34,329 --> 00:02:36,480
I didn’t mean it, Dad.

52
00:02:37,130 --> 00:02:39,280
I was just trying to protect Phrao.

53
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:41,420
I know, sweetie.

54
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:42,900
Don’t you worry.

55
00:02:43,770 --> 00:02:50,020
No matter what happens, I will always be here to protect you.

56
00:02:51,370 --> 00:02:52,170
Okay?

57
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:57,620
It’s all right.

58
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:01,750
Doctor.

59
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,380
Yes?

60
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:05,380
Doctor, how is my aunt doing?

61
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:07,720
The patient is safe now.

62
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:13,150
She passed out due to high blood pressure caused by a sudden stress.

63
00:03:13,470 --> 00:03:15,080
But her condition is stable now.

64
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:18,180
I suggest she should be kept here for observation tonight.

65
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:20,480
- Okay.
- Thank you.

66
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:21,720
Thank you, Doctor.

67
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:23,050
Don't worry.

68
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:34,450
She’ll be all right. Don’t worry, sweetie.

69
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,750
[Door opening]

70
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:39,820
Go get some rest.

71
00:04:40,330 --> 00:04:41,850
You can come back again tomorrow.

72
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,520
But I’m worried about her.

73
00:04:50,530 --> 00:04:52,280
The doctor already gave her sleeping pills.

74
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:54,820
She’ll probably wake up again tomorrow morning.

75
00:04:56,070 --> 00:05:01,520
I’ve hired a private nurse to look after her tonight. Please don’t worry.

76
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,350
Trust me, girl.

77
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:05,650
Go get some rest.

78
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,520
How is Miss Panee doing?

79
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:36,150
She’s okay now.

80
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:39,120
You go on and talk to her.

81
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,450
I’ll go upstairs first.

82
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:51,780
Aunt Nee is all right now, don’t worry.

83
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,980
I was worried sick about her.

84
00:05:58,870 --> 00:06:01,020
I’m sorry I made you feel that way.

85
00:06:06,530 --> 00:06:08,620
It’s me who has to say sorry.

86
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:12,770
I’m sorry.

87
00:06:23,730 --> 00:06:27,550
Phi Jah, do you want to go for a walk?

88
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:43,820
I don’t like it at all.

89
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,130
I’m worried about Aunt Nee.

90
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,770
But I also care about you.

91
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:56,980
If you ever have to choose,

92
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,780
please choose Aunt Nee first.

93
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:03,930
Why?

94
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:10,620
I know how much you love her.

95
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:17,280
I don’t want to be the cause that makes you two fall out.

96
00:07:20,470 --> 00:07:22,130
I do love her a lot.

97
00:07:24,370 --> 00:07:27,050
But I’m not going to let anyone take you away from me.

98
00:07:30,730 --> 00:07:32,200
There’s no making choices.

99
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,670
I’m not going to choose anyone.

100
00:07:47,370 --> 00:07:48,850
What if one day,

101
00:07:50,530 --> 00:07:52,450
you really have to choose?

102
00:08:42,530 --> 00:08:44,700
Then, I’m going to choose our happiness.

103
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:55,770
I promise I’ll never make you cry again.

104
00:09:01,730 --> 00:09:02,920
Phi Jah.

105
00:11:13,530 --> 00:11:15,670
Maybe you should go in alone.

106
00:11:17,170 --> 00:11:18,000
I’m scared.

107
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:24,330
I’m right here.

108
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:31,930
I’m not going to let you face anything like that alone again.

109
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,450
[Door knocking]

110
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:12,080
Aunt Nee, I brought Phrao to visit you.

111
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:14,330
She wants to apologise.

112
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,280
Get her out of my face.

113
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,130
Aunt Nee.

114
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:30,280
I said get out!

115
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:34,380
Do you want me to die right here on this bed?

116
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:45,850
[A vase shattering]

117
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,150
I’d better go wait outside.

118
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,800
In the end,

119
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,280
you chose her…

120
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:42,800
not me.

121
00:13:44,930 --> 00:13:48,320
It’s not like that at all. I love you the most.

122
00:13:50,170 --> 00:13:55,020
Love? Then, why are you doing this to me?

123
00:13:57,070 --> 00:13:58,200
Why her?

124
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,880
That girl is the cause of all this shit.

125
00:14:06,270 --> 00:14:07,900
But I love her.

126
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:11,950
I genuinely love her.

127
00:14:22,970 --> 00:14:24,330
You said you love her,

128
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,650
not me.

129
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,980
I’ve cared for you

130
00:14:46,870 --> 00:14:48,950
since your mother passed away.

131
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:56,050
But you’re leaving me for someone who’s just come into your life.

132
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,520
I’ve already lost Kwan.

133
00:15:05,770 --> 00:15:08,220
I can’t afford to lose you too.

134
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:19,920
You wish I'd rather be dead, don’t you?

135
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:25,480
No, don’t say that, Aunt Nee.

136
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:39,850
Then, you must choose.

137
00:15:43,970 --> 00:15:45,680
It’s either me or her.

138
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:56,330
If you insist you’ll choose her,

139
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:05,180
then go on and prepare a funeral for me.

140
00:16:37,170 --> 00:16:40,850
Phi Jah, how was it?

141
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:42,850
Is she still upset?

142
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:50,700
Just a little.

143
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
But you don’t look quite well.

144
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:59,550
Are you sure everything is okay?

145
00:17:04,099 --> 00:17:05,980
I just feel bad for her.

146
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:10,470
Let’s go home.

147
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:14,700
Okay.

148
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:36,770
Nod!

149
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,470
I already heard what happened.

150
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,370
Are you okay?

151
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:52,880
I’m fine.

152
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:56,670
But I’m more worried about Fai.

153
00:17:58,270 --> 00:18:00,120
If this is too much for you,

154
00:18:00,870 --> 00:18:03,650
why don’t you move to work in Bangkok with me?

155
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:08,270
I don’t think Miss Panee will ever accept you.

156
00:18:19,370 --> 00:18:21,280
I’ll take care of you.

157
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:34,950
I really appreciate it, Nod.

158
00:18:36,770 --> 00:18:38,770
But I can’t leave Fai here alone.

159
00:18:45,070 --> 00:18:49,780
If I’m going to move there, it must be because we both agree to it.

160
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:10,550
About what you told me that you like me,

161
00:19:13,770 --> 00:19:16,450
I’m afraid I can’t accept your feelings.

162
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:27,280
You’re my best fried, Nod.

163
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,750
And also the person I trust the most.

164
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:35,970
But that’s all I can give you.

165
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,770
It’s all right, Phrao.

166
00:19:47,130 --> 00:19:52,920
No matter what happens, we’ll always be friends.

167
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:04,050
I will always be there for you like I’ve always been.

168
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:10,570
Thank you, Nod.

169
00:21:06,870 --> 00:21:08,920
Where were you drifting off to?

170
00:21:09,070 --> 00:21:10,280
A penny for your thoughts?

171
00:21:13,670 --> 00:21:17,150
I was just thinking about work.

172
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:19,730
Let me see.

173
00:21:26,670 --> 00:21:28,450
You’re such a bad liar.

174
00:21:36,930 --> 00:21:41,180
Tell me honestly, Aunt Nee still doesn’t approve of us, does she?

175
00:21:51,930 --> 00:21:54,220
But there’s no way I’d break up with you.

176
00:21:59,300 --> 00:22:00,570
Me too.

177
00:22:02,170 --> 00:22:07,380
The only person who can separate us is either you or me.

178
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:10,180
Your aunt can never break us apart.

179
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,520
I won’t let her.

180
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:21,700
I thought you’d play the angel card and told me to pick Aunt Nee.

181
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:25,580
I’ll do everything I can…

182
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:30,180
to prove myself to your aunt and make her finally accept me.

183
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:37,750
Just like how you’ve accepted that you love me.

184
00:22:50,530 --> 00:22:52,970
But what actually worries me right now

185
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:57,200
is that if I choose you,

186
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,950
Aunt Nee said she’d kill herself.

187
00:23:21,930 --> 00:23:22,900
Yes, Dad?

188
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,620
Are you serious?

189
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:43,980
Your aunt tried to commit a suiside this morning.

190
00:23:44,570 --> 00:23:46,450
The nurse got there in time to save her.

191
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,250
So, the doctor has sent a psychiatrist to talk to your aunt.

192
00:23:56,170 --> 00:24:01,250
The doctor said her condition is getting worse and it might escalate.

193
00:24:01,750 --> 00:24:07,080
I guess it’s time she should get proper therapy with a psychiatrist.

194
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:30,880
I’m such a terrible niece to never notice her illness.

195
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:37,520
Listen,

196
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:42,420
you’ve been an amazing niece all this time.

197
00:24:43,930 --> 00:24:45,650
It’s rather your aunt…

198
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,720
who has been too obsessed with you.

199
00:24:56,370 --> 00:24:58,320
I just don’t get it.

200
00:25:00,300 --> 00:25:02,100
Why is she so unhappy

201
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:05,900
to see me being in love?

202
00:25:10,530 --> 00:25:12,120
She loves you…

203
00:25:14,150 --> 00:25:15,980
and your mother so much.

204
00:25:19,870 --> 00:25:22,720
They grew up having only each other.

205
00:25:32,100 --> 00:25:34,650
I actually feel sorry for her.

206
00:25:44,700 --> 00:25:48,450
She got married to a horrible man.

207
00:25:49,870 --> 00:25:51,600
And ended up getting a divorce.

208
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:55,450
She was disappointed in love so many times

209
00:25:56,700 --> 00:25:59,220
that she had tried to kill herself before.

210
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:04,120
Luckily, your mum was there to save her.

211
00:26:09,870 --> 00:26:11,280
That’s why your mother

212
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:20,050
meant the world to your aunt.

213
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:23,620
When your mother married me

214
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:27,580
and had you,

215
00:26:34,730 --> 00:26:37,280
your aunt always came to help take care of you.

216
00:26:45,070 --> 00:26:47,450
But after your mother passed away,

217
00:26:53,530 --> 00:26:55,220
she was so lost.

218
00:26:57,800 --> 00:26:59,880
She thought she had no one left.

219
00:27:07,100 --> 00:27:08,320
But somehow,

220
00:27:12,870 --> 00:27:14,950
she still has you.

221
00:27:22,780 --> 00:27:25,320
Looking so good!

222
00:27:27,930 --> 00:27:29,950
You’re her anchor–

223
00:27:32,330 --> 00:27:34,550
her everything in life.

224
00:27:38,900 --> 00:27:40,680
But then you fall in love with Kaphrao.

225
00:27:43,670 --> 00:27:46,780
And she’s afraid she might lose all the love you have for her.

226
00:27:49,330 --> 00:27:50,680
That’s why, sweetie.

227
00:27:52,570 --> 00:27:53,900
I also never thought

228
00:27:55,570 --> 00:28:01,450
that the love she has for you could hurt other people this much.

229
00:28:17,470 --> 00:28:21,220
Maybe after seeing a psychiatrist for a while,

230
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:23,620
she might get better.

231
00:28:26,500 --> 00:28:27,300
Yes.

232
00:28:30,170 --> 00:28:32,020
But the problem is…

233
00:28:33,970 --> 00:28:37,980
the doctor told me that for now,

234
00:28:38,850 --> 00:28:45,080
we should keep her away from whatever that arouses her to be like this.

235
00:28:50,350 --> 00:28:51,650
And that’s Kaphrao.

236
00:29:19,470 --> 00:29:20,820
Hang in there, my girl.

237
00:29:43,130 --> 00:29:47,080
[Panee]: Are you going to leave me for someone who’s just come into your life?

238
00:29:47,130 --> 00:29:49,680
I can’t afford to lose you too.

239
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:54,330
[Phrao]: I’ll do everything to prove myself to her and make her accept me.

240
00:31:20,730 --> 00:31:25,400
Dad said Aunt Nee might need to see a psychiatrist.

241
00:31:26,570 --> 00:31:27,880
I think that’s a good idea.

242
00:31:28,930 --> 00:31:33,080
Whether your aunt said that because she really meant it or just to get your attention,

243
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:35,480
it’s seriously concerning.

244
00:31:44,330 --> 00:31:46,330
But I’m worried about you too.

245
00:31:51,130 --> 00:31:52,130
Actually,

246
00:31:54,370 --> 00:31:56,800
I also have something to tell you.

247
00:31:58,870 --> 00:31:59,670
What is it?

248
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:06,950
I’ll move to Hua Hin to work with Nam at her resort.

249
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:12,600
Why?

250
00:32:14,130 --> 00:32:17,680
I don’t want to cause you and your aunt any more trouble.

251
00:32:18,930 --> 00:32:21,350
And you can also focus on taking care of her.

252
00:32:24,300 --> 00:32:28,720
If I’m still around, it would only arouse her illness and make it worse.

253
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:41,720
I really don’t want us to be like this.

254
00:32:45,900 --> 00:32:46,900
It’s all right.

255
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:51,920
Right now, taking care of your aunt is your first priority.

256
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:00,780
We’ll only be apart for a while.

257
00:34:03,970 --> 00:34:06,180
I love you, Phi Jah.

258
00:34:14,130 --> 00:34:15,699
I love you too.

259
00:34:49,270 --> 00:34:53,850
[Fai: Came to work alone today. No favourite assistant by my side.]

260
00:34:58,020 --> 00:34:59,320
[Fai: I'm so lonely.]

261
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:14,850
[Kaphrao: It’s my first day today.]

262
00:35:17,150 --> 00:35:21,020
[Kaphrao: Boss Nam is so kind. She has already assigned me to work this morning.]

263
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:27,750
[Kaphrao: No one bullies me. Life is so peaceful here but I’m not used to it at all.]

264
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:49,220
[Psychiatrist]: How are you feeling?

265
00:35:49,330 --> 00:35:52,250
Are you still depressed or stressed out?

266
00:35:53,070 --> 00:35:54,850
[Fai: I took Aunt Nee to see the psychiatrist today.]
I think it’s getting better. I hardly…

267
00:35:54,850 --> 00:35:57,950
[Fai: She needs to be on medication for a while.]
I think it’s getting better. I hardly…

268
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:01,250
overthink about everything like I used to.

269
00:36:02,450 --> 00:36:02,980
Or having my mind stuck in a loop.

270
00:36:02,980 --> 00:36:04,680
Or having my mind stuck in a loop.
[Fai: Haven’t seen you for weeks now–miss you so much.]

271
00:36:04,680 --> 00:36:07,300
[Fai: Haven’t seen you for weeks now–miss you so much.]

272
00:36:07,300 --> 00:36:08,480
Thank you, Miss.

273
00:36:13,100 --> 00:36:15,050
Do you think they could build it?

274
00:36:15,100 --> 00:36:15,900
Oh, don’t worry.

275
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:18,280
Our villagers are quite skillful.
[Fai: I’m so busy these days.]

276
00:36:18,280 --> 00:36:22,280
Construction is their thing. You can rest assured.
[Fai: Gotta help Dad with work, and also take care of Aunt Nee.]

277
00:36:34,870 --> 00:36:39,150
[Fai: After seeing a psychiatrist for a while, she’s getting much better now.]

278
00:36:39,380 --> 00:36:41,220
[Fai: I hope she’ll be back to normal soon.]

279
00:36:50,270 --> 00:36:53,680
[Kaphrao: Today, I took a stroll along the beach where we once went together.]

280
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:03,280
[Kaphrao: Miss you so much, Phi Jah.]

281
00:37:07,270 --> 00:37:09,050
[Fai: Came to the island to inspect some work.]

282
00:37:12,200 --> 00:37:14,370
Wherever I look, I could see only you.

283
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:19,520
[Fai: Wanna get stuck on the island with you again.]

284
00:37:24,170 --> 00:37:27,150
[Fai: We haven't seen each other for months now.]

285
00:37:27,150 --> 00:37:29,550
[Fai: I wish it'd be over soon.]

286
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:51,820
Here you go.

287
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:54,850
Oh, you’re done, dear?

288
00:37:54,850 --> 00:38:00,580
I made this soup especially for you–it’s your favourite.

289
00:38:02,700 --> 00:38:04,020
I’m full now.

290
00:38:06,370 --> 00:38:08,150
Do you want desserts then?

291
00:38:08,150 --> 00:38:10,780
You’ve been eating very little and working so hard lately.

292
00:38:11,020 --> 00:38:12,880
I’m worried you might fall sick.

293
00:38:16,530 --> 00:38:18,950
It’s all right. I’m really full.

294
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:52,680
Fai has done everything the way you want.

295
00:38:53,930 --> 00:38:55,750
Kaphrao is also no longer here.

296
00:38:56,700 --> 00:38:59,320
Why is it that you’re still looking so depressed?

297
00:39:03,600 --> 00:39:05,620
How I feel is none of your concern.

298
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:10,820
It’s a lousy father like you who has always caused her trouble.

299
00:39:11,500 --> 00:39:15,450
I know that in your eyes,

300
00:39:16,620 --> 00:39:18,680
I’m such a terrible father.

301
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:23,850
But I only became a father for the first time when she was born.

302
00:39:25,180 --> 00:39:26,580
But you should know

303
00:39:27,320 --> 00:39:29,550
But all this time,

304
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:31,950
you've never admitted you're wrong.

305
00:39:33,620 --> 00:39:36,250
And that’s what makes us different.

306
00:39:40,770 --> 00:39:41,570
What do you mean?

307
00:39:42,070 --> 00:39:42,970
I already said it.

308
00:39:44,530 --> 00:39:47,980
When I make mistakes, I admit it

309
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:50,520
and try to work on myself.

310
00:39:51,300 --> 00:39:53,780
But all this time, you’ve been wrong

311
00:39:55,500 --> 00:39:56,600
and never admitted it.

312
00:39:57,770 --> 00:40:00,580
You’ve never tried to reflect on your own mistake.

313
00:40:04,130 --> 00:40:05,780
I’m a good aunt.

314
00:40:09,100 --> 00:40:11,520
I’ve loved and cared for Fai like my own daughter.

315
00:40:13,730 --> 00:40:14,970
Do you still remember

316
00:40:17,470 --> 00:40:19,070
when Kwan was about to pass away?

317
00:40:20,730 --> 00:40:26,050
She asked you to look after Fai and make her happy.

318
00:40:30,300 --> 00:40:35,480
But do you think your love makes her happy,

319
00:40:36,980 --> 00:40:39,450
or actually destroy her happiness?

320
00:41:31,980 --> 00:41:37,450
[Phone ringing]

321
00:41:41,270 --> 00:41:42,470
[Fai]: Hello, baby.

322
00:41:44,300 --> 00:41:47,650
[Fai]: No, not tired at all. What about you?

323
00:41:49,100 --> 00:41:51,050
[Fai]: I already ate.

324
00:41:53,070 --> 00:41:55,350
[Fai]: You wanna see it? Sure.

325
00:42:02,770 --> 00:42:04,250
[Fai]: Just a second.

326
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:10,420
[Fai]: Look at the sky.

327
00:42:13,300 --> 00:42:15,520
[Fai]: Isn’t it beautiful?

328
00:42:24,570 --> 00:42:25,720
Thank you.

329
00:42:32,700 --> 00:42:35,480
Your next appointment is in the next two weeks.

330
00:42:39,700 --> 00:42:42,380
You don’t need to come here with me every time.

331
00:42:43,170 --> 00:42:44,930
I can ask Paen to do it.

332
00:42:51,870 --> 00:42:53,420
I don’t mind at all.

333
00:42:54,300 --> 00:42:57,380
When I was young, you were the one who took me to see the doctor.

334
00:42:58,400 --> 00:43:01,080
Now, it’s my turn to take care of you.

335
00:43:10,100 --> 00:43:12,950
Oh, has the doctor adjusted your medication?

336
00:43:13,200 --> 00:43:15,420
She has removed two from the list.

337
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:21,280
That’s amazing, Aunt Nee.

338
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:23,150
I’m sure you won’t have to take any pills soon.

339
00:43:23,150 --> 00:43:27,120
You’ll be as good as new like before, and stay with me for a long long time.

340
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:36,820
I’m just an old fussy lady who complains on everything.

341
00:43:37,800 --> 00:43:40,780
Do you still want to stay with me for a long long time?

342
00:43:44,670 --> 00:43:50,620
Of course, I promise I’ll take care of you as best as I can.

343
00:43:59,530 --> 00:44:01,420
Then, before we go home,

344
00:44:02,970 --> 00:44:05,320
can you stop by the floral shop for me?

345
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:10,080
Sure.

346
00:44:25,270 --> 00:44:27,180
Time does fly.

347
00:44:29,530 --> 00:44:33,650
Soon, I’ll also follow Kwan.

348
00:44:39,200 --> 00:44:44,120
Aunt Nee, please don’t say that.

349
00:44:45,530 --> 00:44:48,380
The doctor said you should try to think positive, remember?

350
00:44:54,330 --> 00:44:56,280
I was just stating the truth, dear.

351
00:44:58,330 --> 00:45:02,180
One day, we all have to die.

352
00:45:04,530 --> 00:45:08,920
And those left behind must keep on living.

353
00:45:14,530 --> 00:45:16,780
I’ve promised Kwan

354
00:45:17,680 --> 00:45:22,450
that I’d take good care of you and make you happy.

355
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:36,950
But instead, all I do is make you sad.

356
00:45:42,300 --> 00:45:44,950
You’ve raised me so well, Aunt Nee.

357
00:45:45,870 --> 00:45:48,120
I’ve never felt incompetent or lacking in anything.

358
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:58,080
In front of your mother, you shouldn’t lie.

359
00:46:03,270 --> 00:46:06,980
Tell me, have you been happy lately?

360
00:46:31,700 --> 00:46:33,480
Dad, I’m heading out.

361
00:46:33,870 --> 00:46:35,150
It’s dark, where are you going?

362
00:46:35,700 --> 00:46:37,500
Bangkok, to discuss work for you.

363
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:42,150
Hey, you can just drive there tomorrow. No need to go now.

364
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:46,250
But I want to, so that I can stop by to see Phrao in Hua Hin too.

365
00:46:46,250 --> 00:46:48,780
I haven’t seen her for months now–I miss her.

366
00:46:49,780 --> 00:46:53,420
I don’t want Aunt Nee to know. That’s why this is the chance.

367
00:46:54,530 --> 00:46:58,050
Up to you then. But make sure to text me when you get there.

368
00:46:58,570 --> 00:46:59,470
Roger that, sir.

369
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:00,700
Okay, sir.

370
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:01,320
See you then.

371
00:47:01,320 --> 00:47:02,120
Text me, okay?

372
00:47:02,220 --> 00:47:03,350
Sure.

373
00:47:03,470 --> 00:47:05,150
Tell her I miss her too.

374
00:47:05,150 --> 00:47:06,080
Yep.

375
00:47:07,800 --> 00:47:09,170
Drive safely, girl.

376
00:47:12,730 --> 00:47:13,920
[Mocking] ‘I miss her’.

377
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:24,220
I’m putting my foot down right now. I miss you so bad.

378
00:47:24,530 --> 00:47:28,150
I miss you too, but please drive carefully.

379
00:47:28,150 --> 00:47:31,480
No need to hurry–I’m not going anywhere.

380
00:47:31,530 --> 00:47:34,750
All right then, I’ll call you when I get there.

381
00:47:35,380 --> 00:47:36,280
Bye.

382
00:47:36,730 --> 00:47:37,530
Bye.

383
00:48:57,980 --> 00:49:01,980
[Phone ringing - Akanee]

384
00:49:08,930 --> 00:49:09,980
Hello?

385
00:49:23,070 --> 00:49:24,980
I’m Atchima’s father.

386
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:28,170
Are you Miss Atchima’s relatives?

387
00:49:29,730 --> 00:49:30,950
Yes, I’m her father.

388
00:49:31,200 --> 00:49:35,220
How is my niece? Is she okay? Is my niece okay?

389
00:49:35,370 --> 00:49:37,480
She’s under doctor’s care at the moment.

390
00:49:37,480 --> 00:49:38,950
There’s nothing to worry about.

391
00:49:39,220 --> 00:49:42,320
Excuse me, these are the patient’s belongings.

392
00:50:19,470 --> 00:50:21,250
I’m sorry!

393
00:50:23,700 --> 00:50:24,500
Panee.

394
00:50:49,580 --> 00:50:52,850
Fai, are you awake, dear?

395
00:50:56,330 --> 00:50:57,780
Does it hurt a lot?

396
00:50:59,600 --> 00:51:01,180
I’m okay now.

397
00:51:05,530 --> 00:51:09,050
I’m sorry, dear. I’m so sorry.

398
00:51:10,900 --> 00:51:12,450
Why are you apologising?

399
00:51:18,770 --> 00:51:21,780
I’m sorry I’ve tired you out and caused you to–

400
00:51:21,800 --> 00:51:26,280
No, Aunt Nee, this isn’t your fault at all.

401
00:51:29,570 --> 00:51:30,850
From now on,

402
00:51:31,750 --> 00:51:34,320
I’m not going to stop you anymore.

403
00:51:37,100 --> 00:51:42,250
No matter whom you love, I’m not going to get in the way

404
00:51:44,930 --> 00:51:51,250
as long as it makes you happy and doesn't get hurt.

405
00:51:51,800 --> 00:51:54,920
I thought I had lost you there.

406
00:52:29,370 --> 00:52:30,680
Get some rest, dear.

407
00:52:35,080 --> 00:52:36,820
Get some rest, dear.

408
00:53:14,100 --> 00:53:17,020
Phi Jah, I’m sorry.

409
00:53:26,100 --> 00:53:28,270
How did you know I’m here?

410
00:53:30,600 --> 00:53:33,450
Miss Panee told me about it.

411
00:53:35,470 --> 00:53:36,670
Aunt Nee?

412
00:53:55,930 --> 00:53:57,220
[Phone ringing]
Hello?

413
00:53:57,400 --> 00:54:00,820
Fai got into a car accident. She’s now at the hospital in Chumphon.

414
00:54:01,370 --> 00:54:03,580
What? So, is she–

415
00:54:03,670 --> 00:54:04,820
She’s okay now.

416
00:54:05,180 --> 00:54:09,350
I just called to let you know in case my niece might want to see your face.

417
00:54:34,070 --> 00:54:36,020
Hello, Miss Panee.

418
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:41,380
You called and told her, Aunt Nee?

419
00:54:43,730 --> 00:54:45,720
Well, it’s a serious matter.

420
00:54:47,950 --> 00:54:49,580
And she should know about it.

421
00:54:56,330 --> 00:55:00,950
Now that Miss Panee is here, I’m leaving then, Fai.

422
00:55:04,600 --> 00:55:06,080
Don’t go.

423
00:55:11,970 --> 00:55:16,350
Fai needs to eat. Stay here and feed her.

424
00:55:38,970 --> 00:55:40,350
Bring it to Fai.

425
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:41,800
Yes.

426
00:56:05,400 --> 00:56:06,270
Phrao.

427
00:56:06,930 --> 00:56:13,080
My arm hurts. Please help me–I’m hungry.

428
00:56:26,170 --> 00:56:27,320
But your aunt–

429
00:56:27,320 --> 00:56:28,720
Pleaseee.

430
00:56:31,600 --> 00:56:35,880
My arm hurts. I’m starving too. Please.

431
00:56:57,080 --> 00:57:01,350
Hmm, so good!

432
00:57:08,570 --> 00:57:11,720
Look, can you feed yourself?

433
00:57:12,650 --> 00:57:14,420
I need to get back to work.

434
00:57:15,270 --> 00:57:19,720
Geez, how could you leave me when I’m still like this?

435
00:57:19,720 --> 00:57:21,880
You’re so mean.

436
00:57:28,220 --> 00:57:29,320
Just stay.

437
00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:31,000
Yes?

438
00:57:33,530 --> 00:57:36,080
I know you two are still together.

439
00:57:37,220 --> 00:57:42,420
The reason you rushed out at night and got into an accident

440
00:57:42,850 --> 00:57:44,880
was because you wanted to go see Kaphrao, wasn’t it?

441
00:57:45,870 --> 00:57:47,780
This isn’t her fault, Aunt Nee.

442
00:57:47,900 --> 00:57:49,980
That’s enough. I won’t hear of it.

443
00:57:50,550 --> 00:57:54,480
Since you’re the cause, you have to be responsible.

444
00:57:58,570 --> 00:58:00,180
You must stay here

445
00:58:03,170 --> 00:58:06,820
and look after Fai until she gets better.

446
00:58:06,820 --> 00:58:08,350
You’re not allowed to go anywhere.

447
00:58:32,800 --> 00:58:34,380
Miss Panee.

448
00:58:40,270 --> 00:58:44,650
Thank you for letting me take care of Fai.

449
00:58:45,570 --> 00:58:50,250
Let’s just say, I’ll try my best to accept you from now on.

450
00:58:52,100 --> 00:58:54,370
You already beat me anyway.

451
00:58:55,870 --> 00:58:56,730
Fai chose you.

452
00:58:58,470 --> 00:59:01,520
I never saw it that way, Miss Panee.

453
00:59:02,900 --> 00:59:07,980
The love Fai has for you is different from what she has for me.

454
00:59:10,530 --> 00:59:13,550
I can never take your place, Miss Panee.

455
00:59:18,070 --> 00:59:23,450
I’m well aware that if Fai ever has to choose, she will choose you.

456
00:59:27,770 --> 00:59:29,200
Do you really mean it?

457
00:59:31,930 --> 00:59:32,550
Yes.

458
00:59:33,820 --> 00:59:36,550
That’s why I’m so glad right now.

459
00:59:37,880 --> 00:59:40,380
Because the person Fai loves the most

460
00:59:41,280 --> 00:59:43,980
finally approves of us being together.

461
00:59:51,370 --> 00:59:52,670
I only did it for Fai.

462
00:59:54,970 --> 00:59:56,920
I want her to be happy.

463
01:00:03,470 --> 01:00:06,820
And you’re the one who can make her happy.

464
01:00:09,130 --> 01:00:11,620
It’s true that I can make her happy.

465
01:00:12,380 --> 01:00:14,220
But not entirely.

466
01:00:16,370 --> 01:00:22,420
The person who holds most of her love and happiness is you, Miss Panee.

467
01:00:34,800 --> 01:00:35,600
Aunt.

468
01:00:40,330 --> 01:00:41,880
From now on,

469
01:00:43,520 --> 01:00:47,150
call me Aunt Panee.

470
01:00:56,100 --> 01:00:57,420
Aunt Panee.

471
01:00:59,970 --> 01:01:01,220
Thank you so much.

472
01:01:31,480 --> 01:01:32,580
I knew it.

473
01:01:32,580 --> 01:01:36,450
That eventually, your sweetness would win over her heart like how you’ve won over mine.

474
01:01:37,770 --> 01:01:39,550
It’s actually because of you.

475
01:01:39,980 --> 01:01:43,480
Aunt Nee loves you and wants you to be happy.

476
01:01:44,670 --> 01:01:48,150
No, it’s actually because you’re adorable.

477
01:01:49,900 --> 01:01:53,280
Phi Jah, what are you doing? Who said you could do that?

478
01:01:53,870 --> 01:01:55,080
I did.

479
01:02:02,900 --> 01:02:06,350
From now on, you no longer have to worry about Aunt Nee.

480
01:02:16,370 --> 01:02:18,700
Is something still bothering you?

481
01:02:21,370 --> 01:02:23,150
It’s about my dad.

482
01:02:32,700 --> 01:02:36,550
He didn’t stop me when I told him about us.

483
01:02:36,550 --> 01:02:40,450
And even gave us his blessing.

484
01:02:41,980 --> 01:02:43,520
But back then,

485
01:02:44,720 --> 01:02:46,880
I did a lot of bad things to him.

486
01:02:49,370 --> 01:02:52,750
I was mad that he got himself a new lover.

487
01:02:53,750 --> 01:02:56,380
I did everything to stop him.

488
01:02:59,170 --> 01:03:02,120
But now, I finally understand

489
01:03:02,750 --> 01:03:04,850
that you can’t help who you love.

490
01:03:11,100 --> 01:03:13,550
He has all the rights to love whoever he wants.

491
01:03:14,180 --> 01:03:19,750
And having a new lover doesn’t mean he has betrayed my mum,

492
01:03:20,250 --> 01:03:23,880
forget about her, or doesn't love me anymore.

493
01:03:32,970 --> 01:03:33,930
Phi Jah,

494
01:03:37,600 --> 01:03:40,150
should we go apologise to your dad then?

495
01:03:42,500 --> 01:03:44,800
So that this won’t keep weighing on your mind.

496
01:04:52,600 --> 01:04:54,720
I want to apologise to you.

497
01:04:59,470 --> 01:05:02,380
I’m sorry I’ve always misunderstood you.

498
01:05:04,930 --> 01:05:10,150
Aunt Nee already told me everything–that you’re far from being a womanizer.

499
01:05:12,270 --> 01:05:14,020
That you’ve never forgotten about mum.

500
01:05:18,400 --> 01:05:19,750
Or me.

501
01:05:27,370 --> 01:05:28,980
I’m really sorry.

502
01:05:45,970 --> 01:05:47,600
I’ve never blamed you at all.

503
01:05:55,130 --> 01:05:56,130
It was my fault.

504
01:05:57,800 --> 01:06:04,380
I was so consumed by work I hardly had time to take good care of you.

505
01:06:07,370 --> 01:06:09,380
I have to apologise to you too.

506
01:06:12,150 --> 01:06:13,050
My girl.

507
01:06:22,880 --> 01:06:27,420
Then, let’s just say we’re even, okay?

508
01:06:37,370 --> 01:06:38,170
Sure.

509
01:06:40,670 --> 01:06:43,120
From now on, I’ll take better care of you

510
01:06:45,200 --> 01:06:48,220
and spend more time with you, okay?

511
01:06:50,500 --> 01:06:52,500
Just act like before, I don’t mind at all.

512
01:06:56,400 --> 01:06:59,170
Now that I already have Phrao,

513
01:07:02,070 --> 01:07:04,180
I guess I wouldn’t have much time for you.

514
01:07:05,200 --> 01:07:06,000
Okay.

515
01:07:06,130 --> 01:07:08,250
That’s what I think.

516
01:07:10,720 --> 01:07:11,750
Right, Kaphrao?

517
01:07:12,130 --> 01:07:12,920
Yes.

518
01:07:17,330 --> 01:07:19,000
About taking care of you,

519
01:07:21,470 --> 01:07:23,750
I’ll leave that to Miss Wanna.

520
01:07:28,550 --> 01:07:29,220
Yes?

521
01:07:36,400 --> 01:07:38,270
I’d like to apologise to you too

522
01:07:39,730 --> 01:07:43,550
for always behaving badly and being rude to you.

523
01:07:46,370 --> 01:07:47,680
It doesn’t matter at all.

524
01:07:49,900 --> 01:07:54,180
It’s rather I who came into your family and made you feel uncomfortable.

525
01:07:55,600 --> 01:08:00,220
I promise that I’d only stay in my place.

526
01:08:00,520 --> 01:08:03,020
And won’t interfere with the main house.

527
01:08:09,970 --> 01:08:12,250
But Dad is getting quite old.

528
01:08:14,370 --> 01:08:18,020
It won’t be good for him to keep going back and forth between this house and that house.

529
01:08:19,370 --> 01:08:21,950
Better to have someone around to take care of him.

530
01:08:22,120 --> 01:08:23,479
Hey,

531
01:08:23,479 --> 01:08:26,350
I’m not that old, you rascal.

532
01:08:26,779 --> 01:08:29,750
Wanna see my marathon medal? Wanna see it, huh?

533
01:08:29,750 --> 01:08:31,080
You’re really something.

534
01:08:31,330 --> 01:08:32,170
- Kaphrao.
- Yes?

535
01:08:32,300 --> 01:08:34,319
Give her discipline for me.

536
01:08:34,330 --> 01:08:34,950
You got it.

537
01:08:34,950 --> 01:08:37,279
What a rascal indeed.

538
01:08:37,370 --> 01:08:40,850
Tell you what, how about you compete with me in a marathon?

539
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:42,020
Do you dare?

540
01:08:42,100 --> 01:08:43,350
Just name the date.

541
01:08:43,470 --> 01:08:45,450
Okay! You said it yourself.

542
01:08:46,130 --> 01:08:47,680
I’ll take Phrao with me too.

543
01:08:48,470 --> 01:08:49,930
Oh, that’s quite a big deal.

544
01:08:50,399 --> 01:08:52,020
Would you like to join too, Miss Wanna?

545
01:08:52,170 --> 01:08:54,520
Oh, that’s even a bigger deal.

546
01:08:55,600 --> 01:08:56,800
I’ll go cheer for them.

547
01:08:57,670 --> 01:08:58,470
Okay!

548
01:09:42,529 --> 01:09:45,180
Right here, the 101 mining lesson–

549
01:09:45,520 --> 01:09:48,180
the first day you picked on me.

550
01:09:50,520 --> 01:09:52,850
We haven’t seen each other for 15 years–

551
01:09:54,670 --> 01:09:56,450
had to give you a little welcoming ceremony.

552
01:10:07,900 --> 01:10:14,280
The day you disappeared, my world just came tumbling down.

553
01:10:16,530 --> 01:10:17,870
Me too.

554
01:10:20,370 --> 01:10:22,720
When I had to move to a boarding school,

555
01:10:23,600 --> 01:10:26,720
I cried every single night.

556
01:10:30,500 --> 01:10:34,420
But somehow it made me stronger, like how you once told me,

557
01:10:34,680 --> 01:10:36,880
that I needed to stand on my own legs.

558
01:10:49,530 --> 01:10:51,100
I’ve had no clue.

559
01:10:56,800 --> 01:10:57,970
You know what?

560
01:11:00,870 --> 01:11:03,050
Deep down, I’ve always prayed

561
01:11:05,470 --> 01:11:08,850
that one day if we ever saw each other again,

562
01:11:09,600 --> 01:11:11,650
you wouldn’t hate me anymore.

563
01:11:15,970 --> 01:11:18,480
But when you finally showed up again,

564
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:21,570
I just didn’t know what to do.

565
01:11:24,500 --> 01:11:29,120
So, I brought you here and kept irritating you.

566
01:11:31,900 --> 01:11:35,820
Just like what a kid would do to someone she has a crush on

567
01:11:36,520 --> 01:11:39,480
because she wants to get their attention.

568
01:11:43,800 --> 01:11:45,220
And wants them to know.

569
01:11:51,050 --> 01:11:53,680
Now that you’ve realised you were wrong,

570
01:11:54,280 --> 01:11:59,020
You must promise me you’ll never bully me again for the rest of your life.

571
01:12:00,570 --> 01:12:02,120
You mean, when I made you dance here?

572
01:12:02,180 --> 01:12:03,280
Phi Jah!

573
01:12:04,420 --> 01:12:06,180
You’re doing it again!

574
01:12:32,100 --> 01:12:33,530
Please marry me.

575
01:12:43,400 --> 01:12:44,930
What if I refuse?

576
01:12:45,100 --> 01:12:46,720
Then, I’ll shove you down the hill.

577
01:12:46,720 --> 01:12:49,120
Phi Jah! Stop joking around.

578
01:12:50,300 --> 01:12:52,080
I’ll jump off with you too.

579
01:12:52,270 --> 01:12:54,450
I’m not going to let you marry anyone else.

580
01:12:56,270 --> 01:12:57,170
Will you marry me?

581
01:13:00,670 --> 01:13:03,330
I’m not going to let you marry anyone else too.

582
01:13:07,570 --> 01:13:08,520
Yes.

583
01:14:40,870 --> 01:14:43,420
It’s almost time for the Khan Maak procession.

584
01:14:47,270 --> 01:14:49,820
Whoa, your hands are so cold.

585
01:14:50,570 --> 01:14:52,380
- Are you nervous?
- Yes.

586
01:14:56,930 --> 01:14:58,980
Wow, they’re freezing.

587
01:14:59,070 --> 01:15:00,770
Try it, Miss Blew.

588
01:15:08,130 --> 01:15:09,170
So cold indeed.

589
01:15:09,770 --> 01:15:10,900
I’m so nervous.

590
01:15:16,870 --> 01:15:20,450
Thank you Miss Rose, Miss Lada, and Miss Blew so much

591
01:15:20,720 --> 01:15:22,480
for helping me with everything.

592
01:15:23,320 --> 01:15:26,880
Otherwise, I would’ve surely been too nervous to get anything done.

593
01:15:30,130 --> 01:15:33,120
It’s really nothing. We’re a family now.

594
01:15:34,500 --> 01:15:35,300
Thank you.

595
01:15:36,670 --> 01:15:37,670
Breathe in…

596
01:15:40,770 --> 01:15:41,950
Breathe out…

597
01:15:43,100 --> 01:15:43,930
In…

598
01:15:45,530 --> 01:15:46,330
Out…

599
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:51,280
Do you feel better?

600
01:15:52,730 --> 01:15:53,720
Not at all.

601
01:15:56,900 --> 01:15:58,320
I’m shaking all over.

602
01:16:05,120 --> 01:16:07,450
[Phi Jah/ Loves/ Nong*(little sis)/ Phrao]

603
01:16:59,480 --> 01:17:02,220
♫Where’s that love people are saying?♫

604
01:17:02,220 --> 01:17:05,480
♫To always be by each other’s sides♫

605
01:17:05,480 --> 01:17:08,680
♫The love that’s willing to sacrifice everything♫

606
01:17:08,680 --> 01:17:11,580
♫Everything even my own life♫

607
01:17:11,880 --> 01:17:15,020
♫Do they really exist? I’d rather not believe it♫

608
01:17:15,020 --> 01:17:18,320
♫I don’t think I’ll ever fall for anyone♫

609
01:17:18,320 --> 01:17:21,480
♫Love? I don’t find it interesting♫

610
01:17:21,480 --> 01:17:24,720
♫Sorry about that♫

611
01:17:25,280 --> 01:17:27,680
♫But then who are you?♫

612
01:17:27,920 --> 01:17:31,620
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

613
01:17:31,620 --> 01:17:34,280
♫Please tell me♫

614
01:17:34,280 --> 01:17:37,380
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

615
01:17:37,380 --> 01:17:40,720
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

616
01:17:40,720 --> 01:17:43,820
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

617
01:17:43,820 --> 01:17:46,980
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

618
01:17:46,980 --> 01:17:50,250
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

619
01:17:50,250 --> 01:17:53,520
♫Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

620
01:17:53,520 --> 01:17:56,720
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

621
01:17:56,720 --> 01:17:59,720
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

622
01:17:59,720 --> 01:18:01,320
♫Is it you?♫

623
01:18:02,920 --> 01:18:06,280
♫Stop right there, don’t make me confused♫

624
01:18:06,280 --> 01:18:09,520
♫I’m not someone who can fall in love♫

625
01:18:09,520 --> 01:18:12,750
♫No, stop–don’t come near me♫

626
01:18:12,750 --> 01:18:16,050
♫Or else my heart would start to waver♫

627
01:18:25,600 --> 01:18:29,870
Fai, this gate requires not only cash envelopes but also true love.

628
01:18:30,370 --> 01:18:33,650
That’s right. You need to shout out loud that you love Phrao.

629
01:18:33,650 --> 01:18:36,580
If it’s not loud enough, we wouldn’t let you through.

630
01:18:37,050 --> 01:18:38,080
Yeah.

631
01:18:42,270 --> 01:18:45,720
Phi Jah loves Phrao the most in the world!

632
01:18:49,280 --> 01:18:52,120
Hmm, we still couldn’t hear it properly.

633
01:18:54,900 --> 01:18:59,080
Phi Jah loves Phrao the most in the world!

634
01:19:02,970 --> 01:19:04,550
Nam, give them the envelopes.

635
01:19:08,170 --> 01:19:09,380
Nice one there.

636
01:19:12,170 --> 01:19:13,880
- Next gate then.
- Please.

637
01:19:14,970 --> 01:19:17,520
What? You guys are also in this too?

638
01:19:17,930 --> 01:19:18,730
Yes, Miss.

639
01:19:18,900 --> 01:19:20,970
You won’t get through this gate so easily.

640
01:19:21,470 --> 01:19:22,270
That’s right.

641
01:19:22,400 --> 01:19:25,480
It’s my friend’s wedding, so it has to be very special.

642
01:19:25,670 --> 01:19:26,850
Please let me in.

643
01:19:27,820 --> 01:19:31,820
Young Master, you used to treat my friend so badly.

644
01:19:31,820 --> 01:19:34,150
You worked her to the bone and said horrible things to her.

645
01:19:34,150 --> 01:19:35,850
How could I let you through so easily?

646
01:19:39,530 --> 01:19:42,150
Then, I swear before my dad,

647
01:19:42,700 --> 01:19:46,850
Aunt Nee, and everyone right here–

648
01:19:47,130 --> 01:19:49,580
that this foul-mouthed person

649
01:19:49,880 --> 01:19:53,780
will spend the rest of her life caring for Phrao as best as she can.

650
01:19:54,100 --> 01:19:57,050
And I will always cherish her forever.

651
01:19:58,370 --> 01:19:59,380
That’s my girl.

652
01:19:59,570 --> 01:20:01,120
It sounds quite promising.

653
01:20:01,380 --> 01:20:02,620
Give us envelopes then.

654
01:20:02,620 --> 01:20:04,420
Nam, the envelopes.

655
01:20:05,850 --> 01:20:07,080
But…

656
01:20:07,800 --> 01:20:09,580
I think this is not enough.

657
01:20:09,580 --> 01:20:12,520
- What?
- Not enough. We want more!

658
01:20:12,530 --> 01:20:13,330
Just a second.

659
01:20:13,400 --> 01:20:15,880
Hey! Stop playing the damn music first, can you?

660
01:20:15,930 --> 01:20:17,580
I can’t keep standing still at all.

661
01:20:19,370 --> 01:20:20,700
Here, just take them all.

662
01:20:22,130 --> 01:20:26,020
And if you still want more, get it from your Master–I’m so broke right now.

663
01:20:26,270 --> 01:20:28,250
- Can I scan to pay?
- Of course, Master.

664
01:20:28,880 --> 01:20:32,650
I’ll let you through then. Go ahead!

665
01:20:32,680 --> 01:20:33,980
Music!

666
01:21:06,500 --> 01:21:07,920
From this day onwards,

667
01:21:09,730 --> 01:21:11,670
I’ll leave her in your care, Fai.

668
01:21:13,470 --> 01:21:17,680
You must take really good care of her.

669
01:21:20,770 --> 01:21:21,820
Kaphrao,

670
01:21:23,120 --> 01:21:25,550
you’re like a daughter to me.

671
01:21:26,480 --> 01:21:31,320
If you ever have a disagreement, try to calm down and talk it through.

672
01:21:31,920 --> 01:21:34,550
I hope you won't fight like when you were little. Right?

673
01:21:39,670 --> 01:21:40,870
Thank you, Dad.

674
01:21:45,330 --> 01:21:46,480
I’m happy for you, girls.

675
01:22:11,200 --> 01:22:13,300
I wish you happiness, dear.

676
01:22:20,200 --> 01:22:21,720
You too, Kaphrao.

677
01:22:22,850 --> 01:22:26,780
Before, I have treated you badly all because of my prejudice.

678
01:22:28,020 --> 01:22:31,420
But now, I’m letting it go.

679
01:22:33,670 --> 01:22:39,720
And I’ll be cheering and watching both of your love grow.

680
01:23:00,530 --> 01:23:02,880
I love you to the moon and back, Aunt Nee.

681
01:23:04,470 --> 01:23:06,520
I love you the most too.

682
01:23:08,970 --> 01:23:11,020
I love you too, Aunt Nee.

683
01:23:12,470 --> 01:23:15,250
And I love you like my own niece too, dear.

684
01:23:42,750 --> 01:23:44,750
[Applause]

685
01:24:11,850 --> 01:24:12,650
Fai,

686
01:24:14,200 --> 01:24:15,650
do the same to her too.

687
01:24:16,400 --> 01:24:17,580
Do I have to?

688
01:24:28,980 --> 01:24:31,250
[Applause]

689
01:24:39,570 --> 01:24:41,320
[Photographer]: Let’s have a family picture, everyone.

690
01:24:47,900 --> 01:24:48,650
[Din]: Closer.

691
01:24:49,380 --> 01:24:50,650
Move a bit closer.

692
01:25:03,370 --> 01:25:04,170
Hey,

693
01:25:05,530 --> 01:25:07,550
give her a kiss.

694
01:25:07,550 --> 01:25:08,380
Really?

695
01:25:08,420 --> 01:25:09,150
Kiss! Kiss!

696
01:25:09,150 --> 01:25:32,750
Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

697
01:25:47,200 --> 01:25:48,270
Cheers!

698
01:25:52,920 --> 01:25:54,380
Yay!

699
01:25:54,920 --> 01:25:58,350
Finally, our little sis is off the market for good.

700
01:25:58,600 --> 01:26:02,000
Geez, you’re saying as if no one would want to marry me.

701
01:26:02,400 --> 01:26:03,820
What? I was just concerned.

702
01:26:04,350 --> 01:26:08,350
With you being so foul-mouthed and hot-headed, it wouldn't surprise me if you’d stay single for the rest of your life.

703
01:26:10,020 --> 01:26:11,220
[Fai]: That’s harsh.

704
01:26:11,530 --> 01:26:15,520
But I know there’s definitely someone who can take her as she is.

705
01:26:16,870 --> 01:26:19,280
And that someone is my baby Phrao.

706
01:26:21,170 --> 01:26:22,380
See? I told you.

707
01:26:22,380 --> 01:26:26,420
Love isn’t something troublesome like you used to believe.

708
01:26:26,800 --> 01:26:28,520
[Nam]: Yeah, that’s right.

709
01:26:29,500 --> 01:26:31,280
And it isn’t something nonsense.

710
01:26:31,650 --> 01:26:33,720
But rather something that brings us joy.

711
01:26:35,730 --> 01:26:38,480
Yeah, it also makes you want to become a better person

712
01:26:38,480 --> 01:26:39,780
for the one you love.

713
01:26:41,930 --> 01:26:45,550
Everything you’ve always said about love is crystal clear to me now.

714
01:26:47,200 --> 01:26:50,130
Din’s love is soft and gentle.

715
01:26:52,970 --> 01:26:55,850
Nam’s love is honest and sincere.

716
01:26:59,470 --> 01:27:02,680
And Lom’s love is warm and cosy.

717
01:27:04,330 --> 01:27:05,500
What about mine?

718
01:27:07,870 --> 01:27:09,880
How should I define it?

719
01:27:09,900 --> 01:27:11,550
Hot and fiery?

720
01:27:11,800 --> 01:27:14,170
- What?
- Well, you’re Fai so it’s hot and fiery.

721
01:27:15,880 --> 01:27:16,920
Seriously?

722
01:27:17,150 --> 01:27:17,720
Yeah.

723
01:27:17,720 --> 01:27:20,550
Geez, you just love to tease her, don’t you?

724
01:27:20,570 --> 01:27:22,330
But it suits her. Fiery!

725
01:27:22,530 --> 01:27:23,520
What the heck is that?

726
01:27:24,730 --> 01:27:28,150
Listen, how about we change it to…

727
01:27:29,880 --> 01:27:31,280
Passionate–

728
01:27:31,780 --> 01:27:33,280
but tender?

729
01:27:35,980 --> 01:27:38,550
That’s it, Sis. It sounds so much better.

730
01:27:38,600 --> 01:27:39,670
But fiery is nice too.

731
01:27:39,900 --> 01:27:42,180
Maybe I’ll keep it for our wedding night tonight.

732
01:27:43,070 --> 01:27:45,680
Let’s drink to your first fiery night.

733
01:27:48,470 --> 01:27:50,220
Do you need a coach on your first night?

734
01:27:52,070 --> 01:27:53,450
Would you like a bedside view?

735
01:27:53,930 --> 01:27:54,880
I’m just worried.

736
01:27:55,180 --> 01:27:56,620
No, thanks.

737
01:27:57,070 --> 01:27:57,920
You can do it.

738
01:27:57,920 --> 01:27:59,280
Stay focused. I know you’ll pull it off.

739
01:27:59,350 --> 01:28:00,250
Yeah.

740
01:28:00,570 --> 01:28:04,020
I can do it! I’m not afraid! I can do it!

741
01:28:15,130 --> 01:28:17,080
Are you exhausted now, Phi Jah?

742
01:28:18,700 --> 01:28:19,570
Not yet.

743
01:28:21,130 --> 01:28:23,680
We still have to do that thing together.

744
01:28:24,200 --> 01:28:26,250
I’ve been looking forward to it all this time.

745
01:28:26,300 --> 01:28:29,380
There’s no way I’d miss it on my wedding night.

746
01:28:29,970 --> 01:28:31,420
What are you talking about?

747
01:28:36,670 --> 01:28:39,680
I mean getting intimate like what married couples do.

748
01:28:39,900 --> 01:28:43,180
Phi Jah, you’re such a perv! Let me go now!

749
01:28:44,270 --> 01:28:47,780
Come on, baby. It’s a natural thing to do.

750
01:28:48,050 --> 01:28:50,920
We’re married now. Why can’t we do it?

751
01:28:51,180 --> 01:28:52,050
No!

752
01:28:52,720 --> 01:28:53,720
We can’t.

753
01:28:54,750 --> 01:28:57,820
Phi Jah, stop it! Let me go!

754
01:28:57,820 --> 01:29:00,150
Stop it! Let me go now!

755
01:29:01,880 --> 01:29:04,050
You’re not gonna let go? You’re not gonna let go, huh?

756
01:29:09,200 --> 01:29:13,320
Ouch! Why are you so mean, pretty face?

757
01:29:13,670 --> 01:29:14,900
I’m going to shower.

758
01:29:15,170 --> 01:29:16,980
If you’re tired, just go to sleep.

759
01:29:19,330 --> 01:29:21,150
Can I go shower with you?

760
01:29:23,070 --> 01:29:25,250
Want me to bite off another ear?

761
01:29:25,980 --> 01:29:27,850
Aww, so scary.

762
01:29:27,970 --> 01:29:29,770
I’m much scarier than you think.

763
01:29:29,930 --> 01:29:31,680
You’ll find out soon enough.

764
01:29:35,670 --> 01:29:36,750
I surrender.

765
01:29:49,180 --> 01:29:51,650
[Snoring]

766
01:29:55,470 --> 01:29:59,380
Phi Jah, are you already asleep?

767
01:30:04,800 --> 01:30:05,600
Yes.

768
01:30:07,000 --> 01:30:08,730
How can you answer if you’re already asleep?

769
01:30:09,730 --> 01:30:11,620
I’m sleep talking.

770
01:30:28,600 --> 01:30:31,920
Are you trying to torture me?

771
01:30:32,870 --> 01:30:35,220
I’m trying to restrain myself here.

772
01:30:36,400 --> 01:30:38,570
I’m not torturing you.

773
01:30:40,570 --> 01:30:41,920
You are.

774
01:30:43,000 --> 01:30:45,400
You don’t want me to get intimate with you.

775
01:30:46,970 --> 01:30:52,920
You suddenly blurted it out like that so I was just…

776
01:30:56,670 --> 01:30:57,750
Are you scared?

777
01:31:00,170 --> 01:31:02,650
Then why did you push me away?

778
01:31:04,970 --> 01:31:08,280
Well, I got shy.

779
01:31:13,900 --> 01:31:15,400
Aren’t you shy too?

780
01:31:16,070 --> 01:31:18,220
Why are you acting like you’ve done it before?

781
01:31:20,000 --> 01:31:23,620
I am. And so nervous too.

782
01:31:26,300 --> 01:31:28,280
But I want to try it.

783
01:31:30,570 --> 01:31:31,370
